# Rejection-order review

Source: `src/contracts/reasons.ts` (REJECTION_REASONS) and `src/submission/submit.ts` (`submitResult` and `decide`). Line numbers refer to `src/submission/submit.ts`.

## run_dir_invalid

Triggered when no run directory is given (`runDir` undefined or empty), or when the resolved run directory does not contain `journal.jsonl` (checked via `journalPresent`, which accepts a regular file or a symlink). Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:86 and src/submission/submit.ts:90.

## envelope_malformed

Triggered when the envelope file cannot be opened or read (`readEnvelopeFile` returns an error object). Decided before the lock at src/submission/submit.ts:100-101, then journaled under the lock at src/submission/submit.ts:123-127 (which also uses this code as a fallback when nothing was parsed). Oversized (> 64 KiB) or non-object JSON is surfaced through `parseEnvelope`'s returned reason at src/submission/submit.ts:104-108.

## envelope_invalid

Triggered when the raw bytes parse but do not match envelope schema v1; the reason comes back from `parseEnvelope` and is turned into a pre-lock rejection at src/submission/submit.ts:104-108, journaled at src/submission/submit.ts:123-133.

## journal_busy

Triggered when the journal lock cannot be acquired within the lock options; `withJournalLock` returns a not-ok result whose reason is passed through at src/submission/submit.ts:116 and src/submission/submit.ts:144.

## journal_corrupt

Triggered when the journal does not replay cleanly or is no longer a regular in-run file. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:119-120 (`readJournal` under the lock), src/submission/submit.ts:171-173 (typed replay inside `decide`), src/submission/submit.ts:232-234 (duplicate retry whose accepted copy is missing or altered), and src/submission/submit.ts:358-360 (`writeFailure` mapping a `JournalFileError` to this code).

## run_mismatch

Triggered when `envelope.runId` differs from the journal's `state.runId`. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:178.

## attempt_unknown

Triggered when no attempt was opened for the envelope's stage, visit and attempt (`state.attempts.get(...)` is undefined). Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:185-188.

## owner_mismatch

Triggered when `envelope.agentId` is not the opening agent, or when both the opened attempt and the submitter carry a paneId and they differ. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:197-213, rejected at src/submission/submit.ts:214.

## attempt_closed_conflict

Triggered when the attempt is already accepted and the new envelope digest differs from the accepted digest. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:223-225. (Same digest with an intact accepted copy yields a `duplicate` outcome at src/submission/submit.ts:247, not a rejection.)

## attempt_stale

Triggered when the attempt's status is `superseded` by a newer opened attempt. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:251.

## verdict_not_allowed

Triggered when `verdictAllowed(attempt.opened.verdicts, envelope.verdict)` is false. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:257.

## artifact_out_of_scope

Triggered when `envelope.artifact.path` does not resolve inside the attempt's artifact directory; `resolveArtifact` returns this reason and it is rejected at src/submission/submit.ts:271-273.

## artifact_missing

Triggered when the resolved artifact does not exist or is not a regular file; returned by `resolveArtifact` and rejected at src/submission/submit.ts:271-273.

## artifact_empty

Triggered when the artifact has no non-whitespace content; returned by `resolveArtifact` and rejected at src/submission/submit.ts:271-273.

## artifact_hash_mismatch

Triggered when the sha256 of the artifact bytes differs from `envelope.artifact.sha256`. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:279-280. Also raised at src/submission/submit.ts:302-304 when the published accepted copy hashes differently from the bytes that were checked.

## journal_write_failed

Triggered when the journal lock throws (src/submission/submit.ts:138-141), when the accepted copy cannot be published (src/submission/submit.ts:294-299), when the acceptance record cannot be appended (src/submission/submit.ts:328-333, after removing the unreferenced copy), when a duplicate record cannot be appended (src/submission/submit.ts:244-245), or when a rejection cannot be journaled (src/submission/submit.ts:351-352). All go through `writeFailure` at src/submission/submit.ts:358-362, except the lock and publish paths which build the rejection directly.

## Verdict

pass

The `decide` function and the pre-lock section of `submitResult` check reasons in the same order as the numbered list in the `submitResult` doc comment (steps 1 to 15), and that order is identical to the order of `REJECTION_REASONS` in `src/contracts/reasons.ts`. Steps 11 to 13 (scope, existence, content) are delegated to `resolveArtifact` in a single call at src/submission/submit.ts:271; their relative order inside that helper was not verified from `submit.ts` itself, but the position of the group between `verdict_not_allowed` and `artifact_hash_mismatch` matches the doc comment.

